    text:"Chinese humanoid-robotics maker Unix AI is expanding globally ahead of a planned IPO, pushing into markets including Singapore and India with deployments in hotel cleaning and retail -- part of a broader wave of Chinese humanoid firms racing toward public listings even as regulators have begun slowing that rush over concerns that government-backed revenue may be masking weak commercial demand.",
