    text:"AT&T CTO Jeremy Legg said the company expects to employ fewer people five years from now as AI and automation take over customer-service and network-operations work -- while declining to give a specific headcount-reduction figure. Legg said AT&T will still hire to govern AI agents and maintain fiber lines even as other roles shrink.",
