    text:"Cohere and Aleph Alpha signed a definitive merger agreement on September 16, formalizing an April framework at a roughly $20 billion valuation. The combined company keeps the Cohere name, dual-headquarters in Toronto and Berlin, and pitches itself as the first 'transatlantic sovereign AI' provider for governments and regulated enterprises that don't want to standardize on a US or Chinese model vendor.",
