    source:{ name:"Hyundai Motor Group", handle:"hyundai", platform:"web", kind:"news" },
    text:"Hyundai Motor Group put its \"Data Flywheel\" into full operation: roughly 40 dedicated vehicles continuously collect edge-case driving data (severe weather, sudden lane changes, complex urban traffic) across Hyundai's global fleet, feeding a closed loop of AI training, virtual validation and redeployment back into production cars. The company is targeting Level 2+ autonomy from 2028 via Nvidia's platform, with its own Atria AI stack aimed at Level 2++ in late 2029.",
